Z||000000||FieroJoe||12-30-2000||10:18 PM||||I was thinking about getting a electroluminescent scanner, made by Varad, from parts express.  Anybody ever used one of these or seen them in action?<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Seanh||12-30-2000||11:34 PM||||I have a blue/aqua one under my rearview mirrors. I also have their power neon cable to do my interior. I like it, looks pretty cool. I wired it so I can turn it on and off as I like, not with the ignition. I even had one car pull over for me once.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I also sell them here, but would take a while to get since we didnt order enough for X-Mas.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-31-2000||12:17 AM||||Keep in mind flashing lights on moving vehicles are illegal in most places in the U.S. and Canada. Even running with the 4 ways on is trouble in allot of places.<P>You're lucky that wasn't a cop that pulled over or you could've been facing charges for impersonating police. The cops tend to get really nasty about that. You could easily find yourself pinned on the ground with a gun in your ear.<P>Having interior lights on while driving is also illegal in many places. Real good way to make yourself a ticket magnet.<P>I'm not telling you not to get such things. just use them with common sense so you don't get busted over stupid things.<P>Myself I like Varad's elecrtic decal. I even have a good spot for one.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||12-31-2000||03:45 PM||||yeah, I wasnt going to have it on while driving.  I was going to hook it up to a timed relay, so it would flash for a few seconds everytime I unlocked/locked the doors via a keyless entry system.<BR>   Im thinking of getting one now, they are on special at parts express for about $23.||||reg||1
